WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.460
Welcome to Key Stakeholder Roles
in EBP Implementation.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:07.320
In the next four minutes, you will learn
how behavioral health practitioners,

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.360
counties, Centers of Excellence,
and DHCS

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.840
contribute to implementing
evidence-based practices

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.960
and how their responsibilities differ.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.640
Implementing EBPs involves
four key stakeholder groups.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.240
Each group has different responsibilities
for supporting implementation,

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.760
meeting requirements
and delivering services.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:30.780
Four stakeholder groups share responsibility
for EBP implementation.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.540
Behavioral health practitioners
complete training,

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:37.500
meet quality requirements,
deliver EBPs, and report data.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.960
Counties coordinate implementation
and support practitioners,

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:44.300
ensure requirements are met,
and submit data and claims.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:47.860
Centers of Excellence
develop implementation resources,

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:51.520
provide training and technical assistance,
and support quality monitoring.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:56.040
DHCS establishes requirements
and provides operational guidance,

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:59.860
oversees compliance, and addresses
policy and payment questions.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:05.510
Together, these four roles
form a connected system.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:09.310
DHCS establishes requirements
and provides oversight.

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:12.750
Centers of Excellence, or COEs,
provide training,

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.330
technical assistance,
and quality support.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:18.950
Counties ensure their practitioners
meet applicable requirements.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:22.870
Practitioners complete the requirements
and deliver EBPs.

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:27.310
You have seen how the four stakeholder groups
contribute to EBP implementation.

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:30.570
Next, continue to the interactive activity,

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:34.430
where you will explore each stakeholder's
responsibilities in greater detail.

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:37.810
Select each role to learn how
practitioners, counties,

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:41.150
Centers of Excellence, and DHCS
support implementation.
